The  interface provides access to the 10Mb/s and 100Mb/s Ethernet
networks via the chipset.  This  driver  supports  the  following
cards:  3Com 3CR990‐TX‐95 3Com 3CR990‐TX‐97 3Com 3CR990SVR95 3Com
3CR990SVR97 Basic Ethernet functions are provided as well as sup‐
port for tag removal and insertion assistance, receive and check‐
sum offloading, and transmit checksum offloading.  There is  cur‐
rently  no support for transmit or checksum offloading, segmenta‐
tion, nor acceleration.  Note that hardware checksumming is  only
used  when the interface is not in mode.  Each of the host’s net‐
work addresses is specified at boot time with  an  The  interface
employs  the  address resolution protocol described in to dynami‐
cally map between Internet and Ethernet addresses  on  the  local
network.  When a interface is brought up, by default, it will at‐
tempt  to  auto‐negotiate  the  link  speed and duplex mode.  The
speeds, in order of attempt, are: 100Mb/s  Full  Duplex,  100Mb/s
Half  Duplex,  10 Mb/s Full Duplex, and 10 Mb/s Half Duplex.  The
